> The original three additional sequence pairs

The default scoring is2,−1,−2, which differs from the original tiny example.
GATTACA/GCATGCU, HELLO/HELP and ALIGN/ALIGNMENT are preserved with that default.
Scores compare these specified alignments under one scoring rule; they are not
calibrated biological probabilities, and comparing different sequence lengths as
a similarity ranking would need a separate model.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/nw_pairs.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<std::string> labels;
    std::vector<double> scores;
    std::print("| first input | second input | actual score | aligned first | aligned second |\n| --- | --- " "| ---: | --- | --- |\n");
    for (auto & [a, b] : dm::algorithms::needleman_wunsch_demo_pairs()) {
        auto r = dm::algorithms::needleman_wunsch(a, b);
        labels.push_back(a + "/" + b);
        scores.push_back(r.score);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | `{}` | `{}` |\n", a, b, r.score,
                   r.a_aligned, r.b_aligned);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(scores, labels, "actual score");
    p.title("Original additional pairs: default linear scoring").x_label(
        "input pair").y_label("optimal score").save_svg("build/nw_pairs.svg");
}
```
