> Admission and interpretation

Both complete byte strings are validated before policies or table allocation.
Literal hyphens are reserved for inserted gaps, while empty, NUL and high-byte
inputs are accepted. This is byte alignment, with no Unicode normalization or
affine-gap state. A conservative guard requires (n+m)·max(abs(scoring))≤INT_MAX
before any signed score arithmetic; unrepresentable input, table and output
geometry also fails explicitly. These guards correct the unchecked indexing and
integer arithmetic hazards in the old implementation.

[Needleman and Wunsch (1970), A general method applicable to the search for similarities in the amino acid sequence of two proteins|https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-2836(70)90057-4]
establishes the dynamic-programming global-alignment method.
[The native Hirschberg report|../strings/hirschberg.mepml] discusses
the rolling-row alternative; the comparison here uses its recorded storage
rather than a report-side simulator.

> Verification

This ten-report batch passes76 CTest cases,22 directly instrumented ASan/UBSan
cases,119 compiled and executed public examples,513/513 scoped documentation
definitions and ten representative clangd hovers. Independent Python Fraction
arithmetic and likelihood/mass reconstruction verify5266 captured records
with43990 checks, including the original Gaussian controls. Frozen valid-input
comparisons cover DFA quotients, byte recoding, event streams, interpolation,
tours, alignments, real-root paths, packing and nested-sampling trajectories.
Ten checkout headers and ten byte-identical installed development headers
compile independently; an installed-header native consumer links and runs. The
batch has42 executed complete programs and42 visually reviewed native figures,
